.TH IMPROV-DEFINE 1 "" "improv" "Improv Manual"
.SH NAME
improv\-define \- Create a measure or LAMBDA from a definition, "Target = ..."
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBimprov define\fR [OPTIONS] <db> <id> <definition>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a measure or LAMBDA from a definition, "Target = ...".
.PP
Three forms: a formula, "Revenue = Price * Quantity"; an external call, "H = CALL(hypot, Price, Quantity)", which refresh\-ext populates; or a named LAMBDA, "Margin = LAMBDA(p, c, p \- c)", which formulas then call as Margin(Price, Cost). The id names a LAMBDA, and redefining one keeps its first id. The SQL(...) form needs a column\-to\-dimension map: use import\-sql. A formula cycle is refused.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\fR \fI<policy>\fR [default: manual]
When serve\-refresh re\-runs it: manual, on\-load or interval:SECS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIdb\fR>
The model store: a file, or postgres://USER@HOST/DB?model=NAME
.TP
<\fIid\fR>
The measure\*(Aqs (or LAMBDA\*(Aqs) numeric id
.TP
<\fIdefinition\fR>
The definition: Target = formula, CALL(...) or LAMBDA(...)
.SH SEE ALSO
